Dear Tom

Kingsholm Tonnage Ltd / Saltmarsh Shipping Ltd – MV Northern Star

Thank you for your letter of 14 October 2026.

My client received USD 184,500.00 from your client on 9 October. All of it was due under the charterparty, for the reasons in my letter of 15 September and my email of 30 September. My client will not repay any of it and will defend any claim your client brings. I note that your client says it paid under protest. That does not change what was owed.

Your letter said that, failing repayment, your client would go to court, because my client had refused arbitration. That is right: my client has not agreed to arbitration and does not now.

Now that the demurrage has been paid, my client withdraws its threat to arrest the MV Curlew Bay. It will take no step against her on account of this claim.

I am instructed to accept service of any proceedings on my client's behalf. Please send them to imogen.pryce@dunmere-pryce.example by email.

Kind regards

